            "review_title": "Review at Izakaya Yancha",
            "review_text": "Justin S\nLondon, United Kingdom374 contributions\n0\nSuperb Japanese food. A litttle pricy.\nOct 2016 • Couples\nReally enjoyed dinner here this evening. Service was excellent. As soon as we wakes in, the whole kitchen team shouted a greeting at us in Japanese. Huge smiles. Very warm welcome. The team call out to each other in Japanese and then handed us over to the person who'd serve us. What an entrance!!!\n\nWe were given a menu in English and our lovely waitress took our order, complimenting our choices which was reassuring given we had no idea what to eat!\n\nEvery single food item was delicious! I can't begin to suggest what to try as so much was so good. \n\nService dropped a little once we'd finished eating. No one cleared our plates. We asked for the bill, and very happily left, again to big loud greetings from the kitchen team. \n\nFor 2 of us, approx 7 or 8 dishes, 2 sake, 2 water, 1 Pepsi = £55. On reflection it seems very reasonable however given other local options / street food, I guess it was expensive. However this was most definitely not street food!!\n\nHighly recommend!\nRead more\nWritten October 13, 2016\nyancha v\nThanks for your feedback to our restaurant. We hope that you had satisfied with the dishes as well as our service. Hope you come back in the next time.\nRead more\nWritten January 18, 2018\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
